From 1418ad2207cc9ca54a525ca90ee9c470f58b1eeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yekai pan <pyk@seas.upenn.edu>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:46:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 14/21] l2r-local: entry 23-f: the pipelines use worklist
 drops; retcon drops unreachable

Fifth step: rrc's pipeline (crates/reussir-backend), the C++ bridge
pipeline and the C API switch RecordDropKind::Worklist records from
retcon coroutines to worklist drops (23-d, 23-e). TailLoop and Direct
records are unchanged, and TPDE mode keeps plain recursive drops, as
before.

- C API: reussirCreateAcquireDropExpansionPass's last parameter is now
  `worklistDrops` (was `retconDrops`); reussir-backend-sys renames it to
  match, and rrc's pipeline passes the same value as before (on except
  under TPDE). The bridge pipeline sets worklistDrops where it set
  retconDrops. No driver can ask for retcon drops any more; the retcon
  lowering, its LLVM passes and the runtime executor stay, reachable
  only through reussir-opt's `retcon-drops` option and their own tests,
  until they are deleted.

Updated tests (what rrc emits for a recursive enum):
- codegen/retcon_drop_targets.rr: on the seven targets, the entry, walk
  and release functions and the drop stack calls, instead of the retcon
  callbacks;
- codegen/executable_pic_default_retcon.rr: the program passes a glue
  address to the drop stack (instead of holding a retcon table); still no
  text relocations;
- frontend/coff_comdat.rr: the outlined drop of `Tree` is
  `...TreeE.worklist` (comdat on COFF, none on Mach-O);
- frontend/retcon_drop.rr: -O aggressive defers the dead boxes
  (instead of the deferred-free action); its runs (10^5-deep trees,
  forests, chains, locked cells on a 256 KiB stack) and the ASan run
  (sanitizer/e2e/retcon_drop.rr) pass unchanged.
